    {
      "id": 229301,
      "name": "bolnerap",
      "username": "bolnerap",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-12-05T23:08:38.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>By the time Idolator came out, I had several ways of destroying things of 4 HP or fewer, plus the EMP cannon was available,&nbsp;so I just popped him and moved on with life.</p>\n<p>I had a very, very easy game and won with full HP. My thoughts on looking at the initial board state were these:</p>\n<p>- Hey, Chronological Hotspot. I have two healers, I can soak the damage from that. Let's leave La Capitan alone for a while.</p>\n<p>- Tempersonation, however, can eat a fist to the face from the Sentinels turn 1 and I'll figure them out later.</p>\n<p>\"Figure them out later\" meant having Caliginous Form, Hippocratic Oath, and Durasteel Chains out in short order... but I honestly should have left C. Form in the deck because I needed cards more than I needed DR. But it didn't really matter that much - the security droids were giving me bigger hits than anything else because CI Writhe was constantly shielding the people with the highest HP and/or himself. My team got plenty of damage together quickly and took out the enemies as follows:</p>\n<p>Anvil, Anvil, Anvil (AND STAY DOWN), Biomancer, Fright Train, Hammer, Operative, La Capitan.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:00.976Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
